      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Character Sheet identity workflow.\n\n1. Load four useful head/upper-body views plus one full-body view of the SAME person.\n2. Krea2 CcC Character Sheet composes them deterministically into a 1024x1024 sheet.\n3. Preview the sheet before generation.\n4. The sheet is used as ONE Visual Reference with reference_fit=native. It does not define target geometry.\n5. The scene image defines target dimensions/aspect through Krea2 CcC Latent.\n6. Qwen sees the character sheet at up to 1024px so the multiple identity views remain readable.\n7. The prompt explicitly tells Krea to treat all sheet panels as the same person and to ignore sheet clothing/accessories.\n\nCharacter Sheet settings:\n- 4 heads + 1 body (2x2 + 1)\n- 1024x1024\n- contain\n- padding 8\n- outer margin 8\n- white background\n\nVisual reference order is scene -> character sheet.\nScene boost: 1.0\nCharacter sheet boost: 4.0\nCharacter sheet reference fit: native.\n\nThe character sheet is a reference frame with its own /16-compatible grid; it is NOT resized to the Krea target preset."
      ],
      "title": "Workflow Notes"
    }
  ],
